# Line endings are pinned here rather than left to each clone's core.autocrlf.
#
# Without this file, a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true has a CRLF working
# tree while git stores LF, and `gofmt -l .` reports every Go file as
# misformatted — 29 of 58, 21 of them pure CRLF artifacts. That noise hid real
# formatting drift and would make the CI fmt gate either unusable or falsely
# green depending on the runner's OS.

# Default: git decides what is text, and text checks out with LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the formats the repo actually contains, so the rule does not
# depend on git's content heuristic.
*.go     text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.yml    text eol=lf
*.yaml   text eol=lf
*.sh     text eol=lf
go.mod   text eol=lf
go.sum   text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf

# PowerShell is Windows-native tooling, and some older hosts mishandle LF-only
# script files, so its scripts stay CRLF in the working tree.
*.ps1    text eol=crlf
